\paragraph{Measurement attenuation vs.\ construct divergence.}
An equally plausible interpretation is that Likert and pairwise modes measure fundamentally different constructs: Likert captures absolute quality difference while pairwise captures ordinal preference.
Under this view, the divergence reflects construct difference rather than measurement failure---the two formats answer different questions about the same data.
We cannot definitively distinguish these interpretations; however, both lead to the same practical conclusion: practitioners relying on Likert audits will systematically miss style preferences that drive pairwise-based alignment pipelines (RLHF, DPO), regardless of whether the gap arises from attenuation or construct mismatch.

